    "q-97905": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97905",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\int -\\frac{15}{|5x+10|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5}}\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+5 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}+5 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int -\\frac{15}{|5x-10|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\int \\frac{15}{5|x+2|\\sqrt{1+(x+2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=-3\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{1+(x+2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=x+2.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-3\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{1+(x+2)^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =-3\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡u+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
