    "q-97910": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97910",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{16-(3x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we note that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{16-(3x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{16-16(\\frac{1}{16}(3x+2)^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{1}{4}(3x+2))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{16}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\frac{3x+2}{4})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|\\frac{3x+2}{4}|>1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
